@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
allowmixing
hide circle
hide empty methods
title G3 · Access structure: two paths for one synthetic getter
top to bottom direction
class "read_count\nSemantic declaration" as getter {
  example::objects, version 1
  Same whole getter contract on either path
}
class "objc_like\nMessage access path" as message {
  via: currentCount
  convention: object-message
  {field} mapping: identity (implicit receiver)
  compatibility: stable fixture domain
}
class "swift_like\nSource-call access path" as source {
  via: Outer.Counter.currentCount.get
  convention: source
  mapping: identity
  compatibility: source, fixture-build
}
$catalogue(abi, "native · Synthetic ABI entry\nexample.fixture-abi, version 1\nSynthetic digest: sha256: + 64 b digits")
$catalogue(profile, "fixture · Synthetic profile entry\nexample.fixture, version 1\nSynthetic digest: sha256: + 64 a digits")
getter --> message : offers in test
getter --> source : offers in test
message --> abi : selects object-message
source --> abi : selects source
message --> profile : uses message mechanism
source --> profile : uses source-call mechanism
note top of getter
  The consumer selects explicitly or by configuration policy.
  Path order supplies no preference.
end note
note bottom of profile
  test: fixture64; fixture 1; fixture-compiler 1.
  fixture-build pins the source build recipe;
  it does not promise independent binary interoperability.
end note
legend bottom
  Synthetic fixture only, not real Objective-C or Swift support. Non-normative: A2, A4, F1.
  Compartmented box = contract item; cylinder = catalogue definition.
  Labelled arrows show path alternatives and definition selection, not runtime order.
  Both paths preserve the whole contract; native calling algorithms are omitted.
endlegend
@enduml
